14390 IF L22$ <> "a" THEN GOTO 14420
14400 LOCATE 1, 1
14410 PRINT "Your no match for him in fair combat!       "
14420 IF L22$ <> "l" THEN GOTO 14450
14430 LOCATE 1, 1
14440 PRINT "The mental patient is preparing to kill you!"
14450 RETURN 'PASS2-RECON: non-inject verbs RETURN to the main loop (handler is GOSUB'd at 7640 -> 7650 GOTO 7050). Covers the 'l'/'a'/'u'-no-syringe messages (14380/14410/14440) AND 'x' after leaving the inventory. Was GOTO 2440, which RE-ENTERED the inventory - you couldn't exit during the encounter. Only (u + syringe 35) at 14340-14350 reaches the inject.
14460 SOUND L95, .2
14470 SOUND L87, .5
14480 SOUND 32676, 2
14490 SOUND L95, .2
14500 SOUND L87, .5
14510 I272 = 2
14520 LOCATE 1, 1
14530 PRINT "You quickly inject him and he crumbles into a distorted heap. "
14540 L22$ = "n"
14550 PUT (135, 135), I404, XOR 'PASS2-RECON: erase the doctor with I404 (the golf/doctor sprite loaded at 10180); was the L278 placeholder.
14560
14570 RETURN 'PASS2-RECON: after injecting, RETURN to the game (handler GOSUB'd at 7640 -> 7650 GOTO 7050; I272=2 now so normal play resumes). Was GOTO 2440 = re-enter the inventory. (5130's smart-room exit also lands here; RETURN cleanly pops the inventory GOSUB.)
14580 L137 = TIMER
14590 CALL DeathMusic
14600 IF (TIMER - L137) <= XYZ THEN GOTO 14620
14610 GOTO 14630
14620 GOTO 14600
14630 L22$ = INKEY$
14640 IF L22$ <> "" THEN GOTO 14660
14650 GOTO 14630
14660 IF L36$ <> "dindead" THEN GOTO 14700
14670 L36$ = "death"
14680 GOSUB 7860
14690 GOTO 14600
14700 L36$ = "smart"
14710 GOTO 2440
14940 IF I192((I186 + 1) + (L191 * I188)) <> 16 THEN GOTO 14960
14950 GOTO 15030
14960 IF ((I192((I186 + 1) + (L191 * I188)) = 3) OR (I192((I186 + 1) + (L191 * I188)) = 21)) = 0 THEN GOTO 14980
14970 CALL NotesSub: RETURN
14980 IF ((I192((I186 + 1) + (L191 * I188)) = 10) OR (I192((I186 + 1) + (L191 * I188)) = 9)) = 0 THEN GOTO 15000
14990 CALL NotesSub: RETURN
15000 IF I192((I186 + 1) + (L191 * I188)) <> 19 THEN GOTO 15020
15010 CALL NotesSub: RETURN
15020 RETURN  _
'PASS2-RECON: lost RETURN. 14940 (inventory use-item dispatch, GOSUB'd from 5020) routes the grid cell under the cursor: 16->15030, 3/21/10/9/19->12840. An empty/unmatched cell fell through HERE into 15030 (the palette + death-music sequence) - so pressing 'a' on an empty inventory slot wrongly ran the death songs + palette change. RETURN = an unusable/empty slot does nothing. (My death-music RETURN fix exposed this: before, 15030's music fell through to END, so it just quit instead.)
15030 PALETTE 1, 6
15040 PALETTE 2, 4
15050 PALETTE 3, 8
15055 DEF SEG = &HB800: BLOAD "map1.pic", 0: DEF SEG 'PASS2-RECON: load the map image (Spring lost this BLOAD - that's why nothing showed). Same pattern as the intro scenes at 16915. Palette set above (15030-15050) is the map's color scheme.
15060 KEY OFF
15070 L22$ = INKEY$
15080 IF L22$ <> "" THEN GOTO 15100
15090 GOTO 15070
15100 L270$ = "y"
15110 PALETTE 3, 6
15120 RETURN  _
'PASS2-RECON: lost RETURN. The map page (15030+, reached as item 16 in the use-item dispatch GOSUB'd from 5020) sets the palette, BLOADs map1.pic, waits for a key, then must RETURN to the inventory. Blank here meant it fell into the infinite palette-flash loop at 15130 (15300 resets I14, so it never exits without a keypress) - that's the flicker, and why breaking landed on 15200.
15130 KEY OFF
15135 DEF SEG = &HB800: BLOAD "burn.pic", 0: DEF SEG 'PASS2-RECON: load the fire/burn image (org BURN.PIC). Spring lost this BLOAD - that's why only the palette flashed with no fire picture. Same lost-BLOAD pattern as the map (15055). The flash loop below (15140+) flickers the palette over this image for the burning effect.
15140 FOR I14 = 1 TO 300
15150   PALETTE 1, 14
15160   PALETTE 2, 12
15170   PALETTE 3, 4
15180   FOR I408 = 1 TO 10
15190     SOUND 32676, .1
15200   NEXT
15210   PALETTE 1, 15
15220   PALETTE 2, 14
15230   PALETTE 3, 12
15240   FOR I408 = 1 TO 10
15250     SOUND 32676, .1
15260   NEXT
15270   L22$ = INKEY$
15280   IF L22$ = "" THEN GOTO 15300
REM error 41 ()
15290   GOTO 15316 'PASS2-RECON: exit outer FOR loop on keypress -> fire-ending music wrapper at 15316 (was GOTO 15320, which hit the tune's RETURN with no GOSUB on the stack = ERR 3)
15300   I14 = 1
15310 NEXT
15316 RUN 'PASS2-RECON: fire-ending exit. The flash loop (curtains burning) lands here on keypress (15290). RUN = restart at the intro, with NO tune - the original fire ending plays no music (DeathMusic is death-SCREEN only, called from 14590). The original quit to DOS here + DARKV.BAT re-ran GAME.EXE; RUN is the IDE/standalone equivalent.
15530 GOTO 16750
16750 GOTO 18680
18680 END
