SUB Snd5220   'PASS2-RECON: GET / pick-up sound (was module-level 5220-5270, GOSUB'd from 6370)
SOUND L279, 1: SOUND L95, .5: SOUND L280, 1: SOUND L88, .1: SOUND L281, .5
END SUB

SUB Snd5280   'PASS2-RECON: walk sound (was 5280-5320, GOSUB'd from 6820)
FOR L282 = 1 TO 5: SOUND L95, .2: SOUND 32676, 3: NEXT
END SUB

SUB Snd5330   'PASS2-RECON: rising tone (was 5330-5400, GOSUB'd from 6390)
SOUND L279, .1: SOUND L95, .5
FOR L284 = 100 TO 600 STEP 100: SOUND L284, .1: NEXT
SOUND L281, .5: SOUND L134, .5
END SUB

SUB Snd5410   'PASS2-RECON: up/down siren (was 5410-5510, GOSUB'd from 6750)
FOR I286 = 50 TO 100 STEP 5: SOUND I286, .5: SOUND L287, .1: NEXT
FOR I286 = 100 TO 50 STEP -5: SOUND I286, .5: SOUND L287, .1: NEXT
SOUND 32676, .5: SOUND L87, .5
END SUB

SUB Snd5520   'PASS2-RECON: warble + random burst (was 5520-5640, GOSUB'd from 6770)
FOR I286 = 50 TO 80: SOUND L95, .1: SOUND I286, .1: NEXT
PLAY "p10"
FOR I286 = 1 TO 300 STEP 20: SOUND (RND * 300) + 50, .1: NEXT
SOUND L95, .2: SOUND 32676, 2: SOUND L95, .2: SOUND 32676, 2
END SUB


SUB NotesSub   'PASS2-RECON: journal-note display, was module 12840-13920 (GOTO'd from the use-dispatch). Moved to a SUB for the 64KB module limit; entries became CALL NotesSub:RETURN. Internal GOTOs/line numbers preserved; the two note-exit RETURNs became EXIT SUB.
12840 KEY OFF
12850 PALETTE 1, 7
12860 PALETTE 2, 2
12870 PALETTE 3, 15
12875 DEF SEG = &HB800: BLOAD "book.pic", 0: DEF SEG 'PASS2-RECON: load the book/journal image (org BOOK.PIC). Spring lost this BLOAD, so only text showed and the bare 12850-12870 palette recolored the inventory (the white shift you saw). The image fills the screen during the wait below; 12930 CLS then clears it for the note text. Same lost-BLOAD pattern as map (15055) and intro (16915).
12880 L137 = TIMER
12890 L144 = L144 + 40
12900 IF (TIMER - L137) >= XYZ THEN GOTO 12920 'PASS2-RECON: holds the book.pic image (BLOAD'd at 12875) on screen for XYZ(=2)s, then 12920+ does CLS+text. Reverted my .5 shortening - that was when the image was missing and the wait looked like a hang; with the book showing, this IS the intended book-then-text view. Tune XYZ if 2s feels off.
12910 GOTO 12900
12920 L270$ = "y"
12930 CLS
12940 LOCATE 1, 1
12950 PALETTE 3, 6
12960 IF I192((I186 + 1) + (L191 * I188)) <> 21 THEN GOTO 12980
12970 GOTO 13070
12980 IF I192((I186 + 1) + (L191 * I188)) <> 3 THEN GOTO 13000
12990 GOTO 13280
13000 IF I192((I186 + 1) + (L191 * I188)) <> 10 THEN GOTO 13020
13010 GOTO 13400
13020 IF I192((I186 + 1) + (L191 * I188)) <> 9 THEN GOTO 13040
13030 GOTO 13490
13040 IF I192((I186 + 1) + (L191 * I188)) <> 19 THEN GOTO 13060
13050 GOTO 13710
13060
13070 PRINT "   The Zombie Syrem        "
13080 PRINT "MPTP this formula harbors  "
13090 PRINT "the most dangerous compound"
13100 PRINT "that will render a victim  "
13110 PRINT "paralyzed up to days at a  "
13120 PRINT "time. The conclusive test  "
13130 PRINT "on human subjects has yielded"
13140 PRINT "promising results.     "
13150 PRINT "    The subjects though are"
13160 PRINT "heightened in strength and "
13170 PRINT "reflexes making them harder"
13180 PRINT "to control. We have started"
13190 PRINT "the use of torture to stop "
13200 PRINT "this problem. It is almost "
13210 PRINT "safer to leave them on it  "
13220 PRINT "permantly so they do not   "
13230 PRINT "overthrow the doctors.     "
13240 L22$ = INKEY$
13250 IF L22$ <> "" THEN GOTO 13270
13260 GOTO 13240
13270 EXIT SUB 'PASS2-RECON: lost RETURN. The use-item journal-note routine (12840, reached via the inventory use-dispatch GOSUB'd from 5020) sets the note palette, prints the note matching the item, waits for a key, then must RETURN to the inventory. Blank here meant the MPTP/Zombie note (item 21) fell through into the headboard note (13280) and chained through every note. RETURN = read one note, back to inventory.
13280 PRINT "The other doctors have become weary"
13290 PRINT "as the research money is drying up. "
13300 PRINT "I have taken the liberty to hide the"
13310 PRINT "rest so they do not get gready and  "
13320 PRINT "steal it. The money is now boarded up"
13330 PRINT "in the headboard of my bed not even  "
13340 PRINT "the servants know about it.Time is the"
13350 PRINT "barrier to the place of the damned."
13360 L22$ = INKEY$
13370 IF L22$ <> "" THEN GOTO 13390
13380 GOTO 13360
13390 EXIT SUB 'PASS2-RECON: lost RETURN - the shared note-exit for the item-3/10/9/19 journal notes (each GOTOs the 13360 wait, then keypress comes here). Blank meant the headboard note chained into the next; RETURN goes back to the inventory.
13400 PRINT "I have concluded another successful"
13410 PRINT "expirement. This time though the other"
13420 PRINT "doctors have become gready and want "
13430 PRINT "possession of the notes. I have given"
13440 PRINT "them to servants and coded the notes"
13450 PRINT "the code book is now hidden so the "
13460 PRINT "other doctors cannot steal my break"
13470 PRINT "though."
13480 GOTO 13360
13490 PRINT "Patient: Naton McDaniel     "
13500 PRINT "Disorder: Paranoid Schitsofrension"
13510 PRINT "Notes: Naton is very nervous and "
13520 PRINT "complains of voices, often talks in"
13530 PRINT "gibberish."
13540 PRINT "ID:12443"
13550 PRINT ""
13560 PRINT "Patient: Havos Lobos     "
13570 PRINT "Disorder: Severe Delusions"
13580 PRINT "Notes: Havos not only see's and"
13590 PRINT "hears things but they become his"
13600 PRINT "reality. He is very dangerous"
13610 PRINT "ID:385938"
13620 PRINT ""
13630 PRINT "Patient: Gary Coleman     "
13640 PRINT "Disorder: Phyocosis dementia"
13650 PRINT "Notes: Gary has become a leader"
13660 PRINT "of the other patients. He has"
13670 PRINT "a fixation with knives and human"
13680 PRINT "blood and sacrifice. Extremely disturbed"
13690 PRINT "ID:485970"
13700 GOTO 13360
13710 PRINT "3/15"
13720 PRINT "The patients have become unruly"
13730 PRINT "I'm afraid they will overpower us"
13740 PRINT "but the research must go on."
13750 PRINT "3/17"
13760 PRINT "The other doctors to have become"
13770 PRINT "concerned. We all are tired from"
13780 PRINT "working long hours and are making"
13790 PRINT "many judmental mistakes"
13800 PRINT "3/23"
13810 PRINT "There must be something in the air"
13820 PRINT "down there it clouds my head. I have"
13830 PRINT "moved my practice to the attic and to"
13840 PRINT "conceal have placed a pit of ash in "
13850 PRINT "front of the passage only openable by "
13860 PRINT "an electric circuit. I have put the"
13870 PRINT "MPTP vials in the upper left."
13880 PRINT "3/29"
13890 PRINT "Doctor Edwards has been following me"
13900 PRINT "I'm afraid he is becoming suspicous."
13910 PRINT "(The rest of the page has been torn out)"
13920 GOTO 13360
END SUB

